    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "We interrupt this lifecycle for a brief refresher on rhetoric and the rhetorical appeals!",
          "textSize": "heading-three"
        }
      ],
      "align": "center"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "align": "center",
      "children": [
        {
          "textSize": "heading-three",
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Remember: "
        },
        {
          "text": "Rhetoric",
          "bold": true,
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " just refers to the way you use language to communicate, generally with the intent of persuading your intended audience. \n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "So,"
        },
        {
          "text": " rhetorical appeals",
          "bold": true,
          "italic": true
        },
        {
          "text": " are the three main ways we categorize HOW people appeal to their audience: via "
        },
        {
          "text": "ethos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " (credibility, authority), "
        },
        {
          "text": "pathos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " (emotion, positive and negative), or "
        },
        {
          "text": "logos",
          "bold": true
        },
        {
          "text": " (reason, logic, data). "
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ]
    },
